# Documentation conventions
These instructions supplement the root hints whenever Goose reads or changes documentation.

- Keep commands copy-pasteable and execute them from the repository root unless stated otherwise.
- Clearly distinguish official Goose behavior from helper scripts supplied by this sample.
- Update README.md when setup, commands, repository layout, or user-visible behavior changes.
- Never claim a Goose session was tested unless it was actually run with a configured provider.
